---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import StartHere from '../components/StartHere.astro';
import zak from '../assets/images/zak.jpg';
import positano from '../assets/images/positano.jpg';

const principles = [
  { n: '01', title: 'The right room', body: 'Not just any room. The room. Corner suite, best view, upgrade already confirmed. The details that make a difference.' },
  { n: '02', title: 'Access, not availability', body: 'The reservation that\'s "fully booked." The experience that\'s not on the website. Doors open when you know who to ask.' },
  { n: '03', title: 'Curated, not generic', body: 'Your trip should feel like yours, not a template with your name on it. Every itinerary designed around how you want to travel.' },
];

const focus = [
  { n: '01', title: 'Hotels and resorts', sub: 'The ones worth staying at' },
  { n: '02', title: 'Dining', sub: 'Beyond the guidebooks' },
  { n: '03', title: 'Experiences', sub: 'Not on the website' },
  { n: '04', title: 'Destinations', sub: 'Chosen with intention' },
];
---

<Layout title="About" description="Meet Zak Winnick, a certified Fora travel advisor with fifteen years in luxury hospitality, planning premium trips, luxury hotel stays, and curated itineraries.">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="border-b border-sand-300 pb-16 pt-12 md:pb-24 md:pt-20">
    <div class="container-site grid items-end gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 lg:col-span-6 lg:pb-6">
        <p class="eyebrow">Certified Fora travel advisor</p>
        <h1 class="display-xl">Zak <em>Winnick</em></h1>
        <p class="lede max-w-lg">Hotels you'll brag about. The intel to make it happen.</p>
        <dl class="mt-4 grid max-w-md grid-cols-2 gap-6 border-t border-sand-300 pt-6">
          <div>
            <dt class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-600">Background</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 font-display text-[26px] font-medium">Luxury hospitality</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-600">Experience</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 font-display text-[26px] font-medium">15+ years</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-6">
        <Image src={zak} alt="Zak Winnick on a desert road at sunset" widths={[600, 900, 1300]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 48vw, 100vw" loading="eager" class="h-[400px] w-full rounded-card object-cover object-[62%_center] md:h-[560px]" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Story -->
  <section class="py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="container-site grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">
      <div class="reveal flex flex-col gap-5 lg:col-span-4">
        <p class="eyebrow">Background</p>
        <h2 class="display-md">A path less <em>conventional.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal flex max-w-2xl flex-col gap-6 text-[18px] leading-[1.8] text-ink-700 lg:col-span-8">
        <p>
          I spent fifteen years working inside some of the best hotels in the country, including the Wynn Las Vegas, the Cosmopolitan of Las Vegas, and the Grand Hyatt Nashville. I've worked front of house checking in guests and behind the scenes keeping operations running. I've seen what it takes to deliver a genuinely great stay, and I've seen what happens when properties decide their reputation will do the work for them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Working in luxury hospitality changes how you evaluate a hotel. You stop looking at the marketing and start paying attention to the things that actually matter: how the staff responds when something goes wrong, whether the property invests in the details guests don't consciously notice, and if the experience matches what you were promised when you booked. After years of watching this from the inside, I developed a standard for what I think a great stay should look like.
        </p>
        <p class="border-l-2 border-clay pl-6 font-display text-[28px] font-medium leading-snug text-ink">I won't book a client into a property I wouldn't stay at myself.</p>
        <p>
          That philosophy is why I became a travel advisor. Not to forward confirmation emails and technically be helpful, but to help clients find hotels that actually deserve their money. I focus on boutique hotels, luxury resorts, and thoughtfully built itineraries where having someone in your corner makes a real difference. I work with properties where I can get you something you wouldn't get booking on your own: room upgrades, resort credits, early check-in, the table at the restaurant you couldn't get into.
        </p>
        <p>My standards are high because I've seen what's possible when a hotel gets it right. I like helping my clients experience that too.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Philosophy -->
  <section class="bg-sand-200 py-24 md:py-28">
    <div class="container-site flex flex-col gap-14">
      <div class="reveal flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-5">
        <p class="eyebrow">Philosophy</p>
        <h2 class="display-lg">Turning your vision into trips <em>worth bragging about.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
        {
          principles.map((p) => (
            <div class="reveal flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-card bg-sand-50 p-8 md:p-10">
              <span class="font-display text-[48px] leading-none text-clay">{p.n}</span>
              <h3 class="text-[30px] leading-tight">{p.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-ink-600">{p.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What drives me -->
  <section class="py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="container-site grid items-center gap-14 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-20">
      <div class="reveal flex flex-col gap-7 lg:col-span-6">
        <p class="eyebrow">What drives me</p>
        <h2 class="display-lg">Finding the places <em>worth finding.</em></h2>
        <p class="lede">I've built my career around understanding what makes a travel experience memorable. It's not about the most expensive option. It's about the right one. The boutique hotel with the story. The restaurant the locals actually go to. The view that doesn't show up on the first page of search results.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-700">When I'm not planning trips for clients, I'm out traveling. Testing properties, building relationships, discovering the details that separate "nice" from "I can't believe you found this place."</p>
        <ul class="rule-list mt-2 grid sm:grid-cols-2 sm:gap-x-10">
          {
            focus.map((f) => (
              <li class="flex items-baseline gap-5 py-5 sm:[&:nth-last-child(2)]:border-b">
                <span class="font-display text-[20px] text-clay">{f.n}</span>
                <div>
                  <p class="font-display text-[24px] font-medium leading-tight">{f.title}</p>
                  <p class="text-[15px] text-ink-600">{f.sub}</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal lg:col-span-6">
        <Image src={positano} alt="Pastel houses stacked on the cliffs of Positano above the sea" widths={[600, 900, 1300]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 45vw, 100vw" class="h-[420px] w-full rounded-card object-cover md:h-[640px]" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Fora -->
  <section class="border-y border-sand-300 bg-sand-100 py-24 md:py-28">
    <div class="container-site grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">
      <div class="reveal flex flex-col gap-6 lg:col-span-5">
        <p class="eyebrow">Credentials</p>
        <h2 class="display-md">Certified <em>Fora</em> travel advisor</h2>
        <img src="/Fora_Logo_Wordmark_Black-Sand_S.png" alt="Fora Travel" width="128" height="45" class="mt-2 h-[45px] w-auto self-start" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="reveal flex flex-col gap-6 text-[18px] leading-[1.8] text-ink-700 lg:col-span-7">
        <p>I partnered with Fora because they share my belief that travel should be personal, not transactional. Their platform provides the tools and relationships to deliver exceptional experiences while keeping the personal touch that makes travel planning meaningful.</p>
        <p>As a Fora advisor, I have access to perks, upgrades, and insider knowledge that change your trip, from complimentary breakfast and room upgrades to special amenities and VIP treatment. Fora also powers your private client portal, where you can browse and book hotels with me.</p>
        <div class="mt-2 grid grid-cols-3 gap-6 border-t border-sand-300 pt-6">
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-600">Exclusive</p>
            <p class="font-display text-[24px] font-medium">Hotel perks</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-600">VIP</p>
            <p class="font-display text-[24px] font-medium">Treatment</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-600">Insider</p>
            <p class="font-display text-[24px] font-medium">Knowledge</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Quote -->
  <section class="py-24 md:py-32">
    <figure class="container-site reveal max-w-4xl text-center">
      <blockquote class="font-display font-medium leading-[1.15]" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.6vw, 3.25rem)">
        "The best trips aren't about checking boxes. They're about finding those <em class="font-normal italic text-clay">unexpected moments</em> that stay with you long after you've unpacked."
      </blockquote>
      <figcaption class="mt-8 text-[13px] font-medium uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-ink-600">Zak Winnick</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <StartHere />
</Layout>
